<title>CANADA: Canada Q1 current account deficit C$1.221 billion.</title>
<headline>Canada Q1 current account deficit C$1.221 billion.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada had a current account deficit of C$1.221 billion in the first quarter, seasonally adjusted, compared to a sharply revised C$545 million (revised from C$1.703 billion) deficit in the previous quarter, Statistics Canada said on Monday.</p>
<p>Statistics Canada said the change of the fourth quarter number was due partly to revision and partly to reclassification in the way it collects data for the current account.</p>
<p>	 (Blns C$, S/A)   Q1 97	  Q4 96	   Q1 96</p>
<p> Current account	  -1.22	  -0.55	   +0.389</p>
<p> Merchandise		+8.31	  +8.00	   +10.01</p>
<p> Total non-merchandise  -9.53	  -8.54	   -9.62</p>
<p>    Services		-2.35	  -2.43	   -2.60</p>
<p>    Investment income   -7.07	  -6.35	   -7.14</p>
<p>    Transfers (millions)    -0.10	  +0.24	   +0.11</p>
<p>				Q1 97	  Q4 96	   Q1 96</p>
<p> Total receipts	   91.97	  88.95	   84.92</p>
<p> Total payments	   93.19	  89.50	   84.53</p>
<p>Note - Figures are in billions of Canadian dollars on a seasonally adjusted basis.</p>
<p>Economists surveyed by Reuters had forecast a current account deficit of C$1.7 billion in the quarter.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
